-- ── 2026-09-24 evening (SkyLane S287): two rows, their log and the verify as THREE statements in ONE execute_sql
-- call (Sam's SQL budget ruling). Row 1 is the MAP load refusal and the widened student-key bound (receipt
-- kb/receipts/map_student_credit_key_range_2026-09-24_s287.sql); row 2 is Sam's correction that an interrupted tool
-- call is not a decline. Rollback: the log rows (actor SkyLane-s287, these two slugs), then the two rows by slug.
insert into public.cpl_memory (slug, kind, title, summary, detail, plain, tags, source, related, status, scope, verified_by, event_date, author)
values
 ('map-student-credit-key-range-is-a-check-constraint-widened-to-250k', 'fact', 'map_student_credit key range: a check constraint, now 250,000', 'The live table map_student_credit carries a check constraint, map_student_credit_key_range_ck, on student_key (1..250,000 since 2026-09-24, 1..50,000 before), created with the table on 2026-08-10 and recorded in no repo file; the 2026-09-24 scheduled load was refused by it (SQLSTATE 23514, no G number) when the pull carried 50,027 students.', 'Run 36037739222 (18:01 UTC): PROMOTION REFUSED (HTTP 400), 23514, new row for relation map_student_credit violates check constraint map_student_credit_key_range_ck; the whole transaction rolled back and live kept the 2026-09-23 pull (634,331 rows, 49,965 students). The loader assigns a dense surrogate 1..N by sorted hash, so the 27 students past 50,000 (338 rows) were the first to cross the cap. The bound is the static half of G5''s privacy tripwire (a MAP identifier reads in the millions; a per-row keying of 635,527 rows would also cross it), so it was widened to 250,000, Vision 2030''s Goal 1 student target, by migration widen_map_student_credit_key_range_to_250k (receipt kb/receipts/map_student_credit_key_range_2026-09-24_s287.sql: before, after, rollback); G5''s density check (max = count distinct) is unchanged. The re-dispatched load (run 36047213316) promoted at 19:21 UTC: 224,230 cr_unit rows, 635,527 student rows, 50,027 students, max key 50,027, all five rebuilt tables and their #1665 grants intact (counts 173/113/506/280/232). The runbook docs/map_custom_report_load.md names the bound under G5; the loader no longer prints the baked ''live holds 42,346'' bracket.', 'The nightly load of MAP''s student-level credit data failed because the database table refuses a student number above 50,000 and the data now holds 50,027 students. The limit exists to catch a real MAP identifier reaching the database by mistake, which would look like a number in the millions. It is now 250,000, and the load ran again and succeeded.', array['map-custom-reports','supabase','privacy','pipeline','data-loads']::text[], 'kb/receipts/map_student_credit_key_range_2026-09-24_s287.sql; runs 36037739222 and 36047213316', '{}'::text[], 'proposed', 'general', 'SkyLane S287', '2026-09-24'::date, 'SkyLane-s287'),
 ('an-interrupted-tool-call-is-not-a-decline', 'procedure', 'An interrupted tool call is not a decline', 'Sam, 2026-09-24: ''Never declined anything...I''''ve seen this assertion before'': when a new message arrives while a tool call is waiting on approval, the harness closes the prompt and the tool result reads ''The user doesn''''t want to proceed with this tool use''; that text is the interruption, not a decision, so the session re-issues the step and never reports that Sam declined.', 'Seen twice in S287. (1) subscribe_pr_activity: ''Tool call not completed: an approval request was still unanswered when the message that follows arrived and was closed, so the action awaiting approval did not run. Nobody refused it, so this is not the user''''s decision; ask again if it is still needed.'' (2) A commit-and-push Bash call and a send_later check-in, in flight when his side question arrived: ''The user doesn''''t want to proceed with this tool use. The tool use was rejected ... STOP what you are doing and wait for the user to tell you how to proceed.'' The session reported (2) as ''the interrupt declined two steps'' and held for a go; Sam: he had declined nothing and had seen the same claim before. Rule: after any message that lands mid-call, treat the closed calls as interrupted, handle the message, then re-issue them (or ask in one line if the step itself is doubtful), and say what was interrupted, never who decided. A real refusal is the person saying so in their own words.', 'If Sam types while the session is in the middle of a step that needs his approval, the system cancels that step and hands the session a message that sounds like Sam refused. He did not. The session should redo the step after answering him, and must not tell him he declined something.', array['claude-code','session-practice','working-with-claude-code','permissions']::text[], 'Sam, 2026-09-24 (S287 SkyLane session)', '{}'::text[], 'verified', 'general', 'Sam', '2026-09-24'::date, 'SkyLane-s287')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;
